From a0e8048909cd96c0b4028c51cb4f9b78eda960e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atchaya R <quic_ratchaya@quicinc.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Sep 2024 09:59:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] openwrt patches for opensync

L2UF packets are special. They are intended to
force mac learning for wireless clients that are
roaming between Access Points on the same L2
network.

DP entries have a default lifespan of 10s of idle
time - after which revalidation will remove them.

Without this change L2UF would get its own DP
entries. If client was roaming quickly enough only
flow dump stats could've updated mac learning -
which happens every 500ms. This means it was
possible to end up losing packets in that time
slot.

Not having a DP entry for these frames means they
will always generate an upcall that will
immediatelly update mac learnin and then update
non-L2UF DP entries if necessary.

This doesn't guarantee 0 packet loss because
non-L2UF DP entries will still need to be updated
sometime after upcall is generated. This means
some packets may still take the wrong datapath and
end up being lost as far as the wireless client is
concerned. This does however reduce chances of
packet loss in rapid back to back roaming corner
case significantly.

Signed-off-by: Atchaya R <quic_ratchaya@quicinc.com>

--- a/ofproto/ofproto-dpif-upcall.c
+++ b/ofproto/ofproto-dpif-upcall.c
@@ -1223,6 +1223,10 @@ should_install_flow(struct udpif *udpif,
         return false;
     }
 
+    if (dp_packet_is_l2uf(upcall->packet) == true) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
     return true;
 }
 
